hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1133","Chapter on what is owed of justice by rulers, 1173 - Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each of you is a shepherd and each of you is answerable for his flock. The ruler over the people is a shepherd over them and is answerable for them. A man is a shepherd over his household and is answerable for them. A woman is a shepherdess over her husband's house and is answerable for them. A slave is a shepherd over his master's property and is answerable for it. Each of you is a shepherd and each of you is answerable for his flock."
